LINES = [{'id': 'rule', 'text': 'In this town, whoever yawns first in the morning has to be mayor for the whole day.'}, {'id': 'win', 'text': 'My grandma Mimi won once. As mayor she canceled Mondays, gave every dog a hat, and everybody loved her.'}, {'id': 'lose', 'text': 'But a mayor works from sunrise to bedtime, signing papers, cutting ribbons, and hearing forty complaints about pigeons.'}, {'id': 'villain', 'text': 'Mr Bruno hates losing. Every night at 4 a.m. he sneaks outside and fake yawns to win. Fifty-two days in a row!'}, {'id': 'rules', 'text': 'As mayor, he made rules. Everyone must clap when he walks by, and the bakery must give him free cupcakes.'}, {'id': 'ban', 'text': 'Then he banned sleeping in. Everybody wakes up at 4 a.m. or pays a coin. Nobody could think straight.'}, {'id': 'chaos', 'text': 'By noon the baker put salt in the cupcakes, the bus driver drove into a bush, and I fell asleep standing up.'}, {'id': 'brave', 'text': 'I got brave. I marched up to Mayor Bruno and told him everybody is too sleepy to clap.'}, {'id': 'speech', 'text': 'He laughed and said, then I will give a speech so exciting that you will all stay wide awake!'}, {'id': 'snore', 'text': 'His speech lasted three hours and was about his favorite stapler. Forty-one people snored, and Grandma Mimi snored loudest.'}, {'id': 'twist', 'text': "Next morning at exactly 4 a.m., the whole town yawned together. Bruno's own wake-up rule made everyone yawn at once."}, {'id': 'tie', 'text': 'It was a tie! And the rule says a tie goes to the oldest person in town, which is Grandma Mimi.'}, {'id': 'law', 'text': "Mayor Mimi's first law: everyone sleeps until ten, and Bruno must hand back all one hundred cupcakes."}, {'id': 'nap', 'text': 'Bruno cried, then he yawned, then he fell asleep on the fountain. Honestly, it was the nicest thing he ever did.'}, {'id': 'end', 'text': "Now the whole town is quiet until ten o'clock. If you ever visit, please whisper, and bring a pillow."}]
